Corrected-run behavior
- Inputs: 145 IDs, 1..145, for each of roadCameraState, wideRoadCameraState, and driverCameraState; 145 rawAudioData events.
- Every output emitted 137 unique indices, with no duplicates or extras. Per-output segment counts were 97 in segment 0 and 40 in segment 1.
- Missing IDs: road `[1,2,100,101,102,104,105,106]`; driver `[1,2,100,101,102,104,105,106]`; qRoad `[1,2,100,101,102,104,105,106]`; wideRoad `[1,2,100,101,102,103,105,106]`.
- Pytest stopped at the wideRoad assertion. The remaining stream counts/sets are from offline parsing as recorded in JSON/CSV, not additional assertion results.
- The input camera-event distribution between segments varies by stream in this elapsed-time-triggered run; the summary explicitly cautions against treating segment membership as a predeclared frame schedule.

